      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-94971",
      ":question/problem": "The test scores of a group of students are normally distributed with a mean of $73$ and a standard deviation of $5$. What is the probability that a randomly selected student got a score of $80$ or more? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $\u03a6(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*\n\n| $z$ | $0.00$ | $0.01$ | $0.02$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1.3$ | $0.9032$ | $0.9049$ | $0.9066$ |\n| $1.4$ | $0.9192$ | $0.9207$ | $0.9222$ |\n| $1.5$ | $0.9332$ | $0.9345$ | $0.9357$ |\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
